      "side": 1,
      "message": "Calling BTIF interfaces from the stack breaks the layering of the native bluetooth stack (btif -\u003e bta -\u003e stack). The proper way to access this information would be one of these options:\n\n- capture the information in the stack layer directly; the stack also has an AVDTP state machine and should be able to deduce if a peer is configured as sink / source\n\n- inject the information from the btif layer with parameter passing\n\n- inject the information from the btif layer with callback registration\n\nIn this particular instance you might pass the `passive` flag from the BTA layer through the chain: `bta_av_rc_create` -\u003e `AVRC_Open`",
